And speaking of up to date, if you have a Java-enabled browser, you can use their score

00:23:26.240 --> 00:23:27.240
post.

00:23:27.240 --> 00:23:31.800
This is a sports ticker, which uses the Java language and brings you up-to-the-minute information

00:23:31.800 --> 00:23:33.360
about your favorite teams.

00:23:33.360 --> 00:23:35.040
Thanks, Giles.

00:23:35.040 --> 00:23:39.000
And now for our weekly summary of the latest news in the field of personal computing, here's

00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:41.600
this week's Random Access.

00:23:41.600 --> 00:23:46.920
In the Random Access file this week, Microsoft released version 3.0 of its Internet Explorer

00:23:46.920 --> 00:23:49.120
browser for the World Wide Web.

00:23:49.120 --> 00:23:55.320
The new version features 128-bit encryption, free access to popular sites such as ESPN,

00:23:55.320 --> 00:23:58.680
Netsports Zone, and integrated email.

00:23:58.680 --> 00:24:02.720
Internet Explorer is available free over the Internet.

00:24:02.720 --> 00:24:06.320
Netscape also unveiled an upgraded version of its web browser.

00:24:06.320 --> 00:24:12.640
Navigator 3.0 has added new features for viewing 3D content and using the Internet for telephone

00:24:12.640 --> 00:24:13.920
calls.

00:24:13.920 --> 00:24:18.960
Netscape lets you download the software from its website and use it for 90 days.

00:24:18.960 --> 00:24:21.560
It will sell for $50.

00:24:21.560 --> 00:24:26.680
As the battle of the browsers heats up, Netscape has asked the Justice Department to investigate

00:24:26.680 --> 00:24:32.480
Microsoft to see if it is using strong-arm tactics to gain control of the Internet market.

00:24:32.480 --> 00:24:36.000
Federal authorities have not formally responded.

00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:40.520
Internet hackers recently infiltrated the Justice Department's homepage.

00:24:40.520 --> 00:24:47.000
Hackers used the site to criticize the Communications Decency Act and posted sexually explicit pictures.

00:24:47.000 --> 00:24:51.120
The Justice Department has removed the unauthorized material.

00:24:51.120 --> 00:24:56.520
Ten high-tech companies are investing $100 million to finance the development of Java

00:24:56.520 --> 00:24:58.560
software for the Internet.

00:24:58.560 --> 00:25:04.080
The companies include the likes of Sun, Compaq, and IBM and show strong support for the new

00:25:04.080 --> 00:25:05.760
programming language.

00:25:05.760 --> 00:25:11.960
Java programs called Applets can be used on any computer with the latest web browsers.

00:25:11.960 --> 00:25:16.480
And finally, what newspaper uses the slogan, All the News that's Fit to Print?

00:25:16.480 --> 00:25:18.320
The New York Times, of course.

00:25:18.320 --> 00:25:23.000
The newspaper is looking for a new slogan to be used on its first website.

00:25:23.000 --> 00:25:28.720
Your slogan must be ten words or less and submitted by October 1st via email.

00:25:28.720 --> 00:25:30.440
That's it for this week's Random Access.

00:25:30.440 --> 00:25:32.320
We'll send it back to you, Stuart.

00:25:32.320 --> 00:25:34.000
Now for my pick of the week.

00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:38.600
About five years ago, I came across an interesting software title called The Castle of Dr. Brain.

00:25:38.600 --> 00:25:40.960
It was a great problem-solving program.

00:25:40.960 --> 00:25:44.800
Then a few years later, there was a follow-up called The Island of Dr. Brain.

00:25:44.800 --> 00:25:49.160
Now, the good folks at Sierra have come out with the best in the series called The Lost

00:25:49.160 --> 00:25:51.080
Mind of Dr. Brain.

00:25:51.080 --> 00:25:54.720
This is really an SAT preparation program in disguise.

00:25:54.720 --> 00:25:58.960
It's great fun, and it also teaches you basic problem-solving skills.

00:25:58.960 --> 00:26:03.560
The program comes with ten different sets of problems in various mental skill areas.

00:26:03.560 --> 00:26:07.800
My favorites are motor programming, in which you learn the fundamentals of writing computer

00:26:07.800 --> 00:26:12.880
code, the train of thought, in which you have to quickly follow directions and design logical

00:26:12.880 --> 00:26:17.000
traffic patterns, and CAD construction, in which you have to figure out how to build

00:26:17.000 --> 00:26:19.120
complex 3D shapes.

00:26:19.120 --> 00:26:22.760
The program is very cleverly done with great music and sound effects.

00:26:22.760 --> 00:26:24.960
You can play at various skill levels.

00:26:24.960 --> 00:26:28.920
Even though the package says it's for 12 years old and above, I think if you have a smart

00:26:28.920 --> 00:26:31.560
7 or 8-year-old, they'll like this, too.

00:26:31.560 --> 00:26:34.400
The Lost Mind of Dr. Brain is from Sierra.

00:26:34.400 --> 00:26:36.080
It's available for Windows and the Mac.

00:26:36.080 --> 00:26:39.080
It sells for under $50, and it won the S.P.A.

00:26:39.080 --> 00:26:42.560
Cody Award for Best Home Learning Program.

